roboparty-rp-server (1.5.5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Boot path is read-only: motors are probed without enabling, and the
    service runs without a robot YAML or hardware.
  * Readiness fails closed when ROS cannot be queried; repeated starts report
    an existing inference instance instead of killing it.
  * Add an explicit developer_mode switch (config or RP_DEVELOPER_MODE) that
    bypasses the cross-process control lock for development only.
  * Keep the legacy rp-btwifi provisioning service disabled by default and
    gate it with /etc/rp-server/enable-btwifi.
  * Depend on roboparty-start >= 1.3.1 and roboparty-inference >= 1.3.0 for
    standalone installation.

 -- changchuanyong <1984715306@qq.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0800

roboparty-rp-server (1.5.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * StopAck separates the software stop from hardware state with
    software_stopped, motor_state and estop_state. The server reports motor
    and E-stop state as unknown because it cannot verify them.

 -- RoboParty <2321901849@qq.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 15:40:00 +0800

roboparty-rp-server (1.5.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep failed log events in a bounded dead-letter table instead of silently
    dropping them after max attempts or a permanent HTTP 4xx.
  * Ack only after a successful upload; expose spool, dropped and rejected
    counters and rate-limited stderr warnings.

